# exit: 1
# Two properties of -noproof past the prefix it skipped.
#
# First, a position outside any proof (the whole file here) skips every
# proof in it: the reply is tagged [noproof] and leaves no active proof.
#
# Second, skipping ends with the LOAD. Proof checking is restored on
# the way out, so the phrase typed next is checked for real and its
# `qed.' is refused -- which is what makes the exit status 1.
LOAD "fixtures/noproof.ec" -noproof
<BEGIN>
lemma unproved : false.
proof.
trivial.
qed.
<DONE>
